---
import DocsLayout from "../_components/DocsLayout.bangala"
import CodeBlock from "../_components/CodeBlock.bangala"

const create = `npm create bangala@latest my-app
cd my-app
npm install
npm run dev`;

const manualInstall = `npm install bangala vite`;

const packageJson = `{
  "type": "module",
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "bangala dev",
    "build": "bangala build"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "bangala": "^1.0.0"
  }
}`;

const headings = [
  { id: "requirements", label: "Requirements" },
  { id: "create-project", label: "Create a project" },
  { id: "manual-install", label: "Manual install" },
  { id: "next-steps", label: "Next steps" },
];
---
<DocsLayout
  title="Installation | bangala.js"
  description="Installer bangala.js avec npm et créer un premier projet HTML-first."
  path="/docs/installation"
  section="Getting Started"
  lead="Install Bangala with the CLI for the fastest path, or add it manually to an existing Vite project."
  headings={headings}
  prev={{ href: "/docs", label: "Introduction" }}
  next={{ href: "/docs/project-structure", label: "Project structure" }}
>
  <h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
  <p>Bangala targets modern ESM tooling and requires Node.js 22 or newer. The package is published as ESM and ships a <code>bangala</code> CLI binary.</p>

  <h2 id="create-project">Create a project</h2>
  <p>The create command scaffolds a working site with pages, a component, an island module, and package scripts.</p>
  <CodeBlock filename="Terminal" lang="bash" code={create}/>

  <h2 id="manual-install">Manual install</h2>
  <p>For an existing project, install the package and add scripts that call the CLI.</p>
  <CodeBlock filename="Terminal" lang="bash" code={manualInstall}/>
  <CodeBlock filename="package.json" lang="json" code={packageJson}/>

  <h2 id="next-steps">Next steps</h2>
  <p>Create <code>pages/index.bangala</code>, run <code>npm run dev</code>, and open the local URL. The dev server discovers routes from <code>pages/</code> and compiles <code>.bangala</code> files on demand.</p>
</DocsLayout>
